    "title": "What channel is the Final Four on tonight?",
    "text": "Michigan Wolverines head coach Dusty May and players celebrate with confetti and the NCAA Midwest Regional trophy after Michigan basketball defeated Tennessee 95-62 in the Elite Eight at United Center in Chicago on Saturday, March 28 2026.MLive.comIf you purchase a product through a link on our site, we may receive compensation.By Jenna Malinowski | JMalinowski@mlive.comThe Final Four teams in the 2026 NCAA Tournament will face off tonight for a spot in the national championship. Here’s everything you need to know about how to catch the action:What channel is the Final Four on?The two Final Four games will be broadcast on TBS and TruTV.What time are the games?The first matchup between UConn and Illinois will tip off at 6:09 p.m. ET, and the second matchup between Michigan and Arizona is scheduled to start at 8:49 p.m. ET. How can I stream the Final Four?Streaming options are available through DirecTV Stream, Sling and HBO Max. Final Four Streaming OptionsDirecTV Stream: DirecTV Stream’s Choice plan offers over 125 channels, including TBS and TruTV. New subscribers can start with a five-day free trial and take $35 off their first month. Sling: Sling offers three different monthly plans that include access to TBS. Unlike other services, Sling offers day passes, starting at $4.99. HBO Max: HBO Max’s standard plan offers customers hundreds of hit TV shows and movies, as well as live sports on TNT and TBS. When is the national championship game?The two winners of tonight’s games will advance to the national championship game, which will be played Monday, April 6 at 8:50 p.m. ET.Where to watch the Golden State Warriors vs. Los Angeles Clippers NBA play-in game free streamHow to watch Orlando Magic vs. Philadelphia 76ers NBA play-in game for free tonightHow to watch the Detroit Tigers vs. Kansas City Royals tonight for free without cableJenna is a sports commerce writer for MLive.com. She writes about how to stream and get ticket deals for your favorite sporting events and where you can find gear for the Detroit Tigers, the Detroit Red Wings,...",
